WEBVTT

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:04.400
Thank you.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.740
You, cook, put the pot down and go to the fire.

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:05.200
I love Lola, Mr. Mayor Domo. Lola!

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:08.250
What a century, sir! Even the cooks have names.

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:11.160
And you, go and prepare the okra. Quickly!

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:13.560
Don't mess with my secretary. Let's go, pirula.

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:14.780
Pirula.

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:20.660
You, ant killer, go and grab the scissors and go and cut some gladiolus.

00:02:21.350 --> 00:02:23.050
You, butcher, go and cut the okra.

00:02:23.150 --> 00:02:28.470
And you, fangio, put the pot down and go to your place.

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:39.340
What are you looking at?

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:40.740
You, Sonsu!

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:42.760
I earned the obligation better than you!

00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:44.560
Why do you have to come and send me here?

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:45.160
You coward!

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:46.740
Salabraja Salai!

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:48.630
Patuay Salabu Alcalá!

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:51.380
If it wasn't because he was the driver of the Alarcán!

00:02:53.050 --> 00:02:54.370
I, sir, I...

00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:55.210
You follow me immediately!

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:56.960
What things do I have to teach them?

00:02:56.980 --> 00:02:57.720
How do they have to work?

00:02:57.940 --> 00:02:58.680
How do they have to dress?

00:02:59.000 --> 00:02:59.840
How do they have to dress?

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:00.840
How can you do that?

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:03.280
How did Pimpollo wake up?

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:07.310
I thought he was angry with me, Mr. Mayor.

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:10.490
For you, my little mouse, I'm not Mr. Mayor.

00:03:10.970 --> 00:03:12.050
I'm Polo.

00:03:12.130 --> 00:03:13.730
Or Polito, if you prefer.

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:14.990
Polito.

00:03:15.410 --> 00:03:15.890
Oto.

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:18.570
And if you think it's too long, call me Oh-Oh.

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:21.820
I like Polo.

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:23.400
Although Polo is cold.

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:27.390
How naive, sir, how naive.

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:32.840
I mean, Mr. Polo.

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:34.020
Honey!

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:37.380
I forgot to tell you something amazing.

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:40.170
Last night my boyfriend...

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:41.410
You have a boyfriend, my little frog!

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:42.480
Four.

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:45.510
Quaterno! How naïve!

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:48.300
What are you waiting for, my little frog?

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:50.270
To make a lottery?

00:03:51.110 --> 00:03:53.190
No, but look how extraordinary.

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:56.030
Last night my boyfriend took me to a cafe in San Telmo

00:03:56.030 --> 00:03:58.860
and something amazing happened to me.

00:03:58.860 --> 00:03:59.620
What happened?

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:04.340
In that café in San Telmo? Oh, I can't believe it!

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:06.560
Are you telling me a movie in an episode?

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:09.900
It's seven o'clock. I have to wake up Miguel Ángel.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:11.680
Then you tell me everything. My love!

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:17.380
I couldn't sleep all night thinking about that.

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:18.200
What a suspense!

00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:19.740
I'll follow you later.

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:22.220
Because I'm going to wake up the boy a minute late.

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:34.600
Well done, Mr. Gaspar, 60,000.

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:37.810
Poor thing, even in his sleep he's worried about the business.

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:41.300
Well done, 70,000.

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:44.160
Mr. Miguel Aires, it's 7 o'clock and...

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:45.920
Well, 100,000 pesos, do you think it's good?

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:47.760
Well, do whatever you want.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:50.300
Mr. Gaspar, one year?

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:52.800
Yes, do you want to buy all the umbrellas and umbrellas in the square?

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:53.020
What?

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:54.560
Yes, he says he wants to be covered.

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:55.960
Like the other day with the screws?

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:59.220
Yes, I wanted to be tight. I swear I'm tired.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.580
A fatso can't be tired, sir.

00:05:01.990 --> 00:05:04.750
Speaking of fatso, I feel quite skinny, huh?

00:05:11.030 --> 00:05:14.240
Always making drawings, genius and figure.

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:17.920
And for what did you want the 100,000 pesos, Mr. Gaspar?

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:19.320
For a fiancée.

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:22.080
How exaggerated, 100,000 pesos for a fiancée.

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:24.420
Depending on who it is, if it were for you, a peso would be enough.

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:29.980
It must be ready for today, sir, to have a bright day.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:33.120
I didn't hear you come back last night.

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:33.560
I'm late.

00:05:34.240 --> 00:05:34.820
Where did you go?

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:35.950
Over there.

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:38.840
What if Mr. Gaspar finds out that I didn't find those exits?

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:40.540
Mr. Gaspar is getting into my life a lot.

00:05:40.660 --> 00:05:44.100
Don't forget, Mr. Miguel Angel, that your late father, Don Luis Gorducci,

00:05:44.260 --> 00:05:46.900
gave you the factory of Faja La Espelta.

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:49.730
But the general supervision to Mr. Gaspar Uraño,

00:05:49.810 --> 00:05:54.640
his best friend, and his personal surveillance to a servant.

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:55.840
How they dry!

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:56.990
How do you say, sir?

00:05:57.270 --> 00:05:59.090
No, how they dry, how good are the towels, huh?

00:06:06.270 --> 00:06:07.850
Very good, very good, very elegant.

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:10.530
Undoubtedly, Mr. Gaspar knows how to dress him.

00:06:10.650 --> 00:06:11.890
Mr. Gaspar, Mr. Gaspar.

00:06:11.990 --> 00:06:13.060
And this umbrella?

00:06:13.420 --> 00:06:15.600
All the great English financiers wear it.

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:16.580
Didn't you see it in the photos?

00:06:16.820 --> 00:06:17.220
What?

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:18.960
Chávez's partner.

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:23.020
It's extraordinary, amazing.

00:06:24.830 --> 00:06:24.890
What?

00:06:25.130 --> 00:06:29.370
Well, let's go to the dormitory, I mean, to the office.

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:30.730
Oh

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:01.720
that criticizes you so much for your debauchery.

00:07:02.200 --> 00:07:03.740
Mr. Gaspar, a year and I'm out of it.

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:05.730
What happened there, Mustafa?

00:07:06.090 --> 00:07:09.660
Didn't you feel that we put a rubber band on you or you're deaf?

00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:11.220
What a man!

00:07:11.480 --> 00:07:14.440
How is the staff, sir?

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:17.140
Mortification after mortification.

00:07:18.020 --> 00:07:24.380
Good morning, Mr. Gaspar.

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:25.180
Good morning. Any news?

00:07:25.480 --> 00:07:27.720
Mr. Gorducci arrived five minutes ago.

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:41.040
It was 10 o'clock.

00:07:51.850 --> 00:07:57.010
Miguel Ángel found the other censor smoking.

00:07:57.820 --> 00:07:58.000
And?

00:07:58.140 --> 00:07:59.580
He suspended him for a day.

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:05.010
But I wonder, Mr. Miguel, what he's waiting for to say goodbye to the plumber.

00:08:05.270 --> 00:08:07.070
He says he was sad and he started smoking to forget.

00:08:07.410 --> 00:08:10.090
But Mr. Miguel, another day when he feels sad to rejoice,

00:08:10.430 --> 00:08:11.810
he can light a fire in the factory.

00:08:12.090 --> 00:08:13.630
Very good, very good, Mr. Uraño.

00:08:13.830 --> 00:08:14.880
What are you laughing at?

00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:16.720
Sorry, I thought it was a joke.

00:08:17.040 --> 00:08:18.500
The same as arriving ten minutes late.

00:08:18.740 --> 00:08:19.940
The bosses must set an example.

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:21.160
A rubber was stuck in our path.

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:22.540
Very nice pretext.

00:08:22.740 --> 00:08:25.500
But let's hope that our strip is not made with that kind of rubber.

00:08:26.260 --> 00:08:27.780
Why don't you laugh now that it's a joke?

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:29.280
And if you don't tell Mr. Uraño?

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:29.980
Mr. Miguel, I'm sorry.

00:08:30.600 --> 00:08:33.300
lf your father had been like that, they wouldn't be where they are now.

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:36.260
l know, Mr. Gaspar, you shouldn't smile, that's your motto.

00:08:36.600 --> 00:08:39.140
Of course, you smile and ask for something, not fake.

00:08:39.400 --> 00:08:41.020
You have to be a tyrant to be respected.

00:08:41.380 --> 00:08:42.100
A tyrant!

00:08:42.360 --> 00:08:43.980
l know, the bosses have to be strong.

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:46.380
Yes, sir, the employee is the son of rigor.

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:49.120
Mr. Gaspar, Mr. Gorducci's fiancée wants to see you.

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:50.190
Let her in.

00:08:50.330 --> 00:08:51.190
You wait outside.

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:53.500
Mr. Gorducci has a few minutes of romance.

00:08:53.760 --> 00:08:54.280
All right, sir.

00:08:54.510 --> 00:08:57.190
Don't forget that this marriage unites us with our only enemy.

00:08:57.470 --> 00:08:59.650
That damn product that has come out to destroy us.

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:04.990
Remember at all times that the father of your fiancée is the king of the Nylon.

00:09:05.130 --> 00:09:09.830
Don't worry, let the queen of the Nylon pass. I will treat her like the prince of the couch.

00:09:09.990 --> 00:09:11.970
That's how I like it. Very good!

00:09:12.390 --> 00:09:17.310
And in case we don't see each other, remember that the meeting of the director is this afternoon at 5 p.m.

00:09:22.990 --> 00:09:26.740
Delicate creature. I see her every day more beautiful.

00:09:27.160 --> 00:09:28.560
Love awaits her.

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:32.240
What a funny guy, Mr. Gaspar.

00:09:32.360 --> 00:09:33.020
Yes, and very human.

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:37.570
I've come to give you a brief list of your guests for our engagement.

00:09:37.790 --> 00:09:41.250
With Dad and Mr. Gaspar, we've decided that it will be within two weeks.

00:09:41.550 --> 00:09:41.770
Okay?

00:09:42.090 --> 00:09:45.910
Great, and don't forget to invite Ilusión, Cariño and Amor.

00:09:45.910 --> 00:09:46.810
Don't be so courteous, please.

00:09:47.270 --> 00:09:49.870
Don't talk about things that aren't used, at least among us.

00:09:50.580 --> 00:09:51.750
I'll wait for that list.

00:09:51.970 --> 00:09:52.720
See you later.

00:09:53.340 --> 00:09:54.640
Goodbye, Amor.

00:09:55.620 --> 00:09:59.970
I think that this salary cut for the staff and Amor...

00:10:01.880 --> 00:10:04.060
because we are giving away the drugs,

00:10:04.760 --> 00:10:07.640
there is nothing else to do, Mr. President, right?

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:09.180
Yes, Mr. Gaspar.

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:10.120
One moment, sir.

00:10:10.340 --> 00:10:12.700
I think we are stretching the rope too much.

00:10:13.060 --> 00:10:15.080
Keep in mind that in the López & López factory,

00:10:15.080 --> 00:10:16.200
the corseters earn three more pesos,

00:10:16.480 --> 00:10:17.780
and the smugglers, 1.40.

00:10:18.020 --> 00:10:20.100
Let López & López give away the money if they want to.

00:10:20.180 --> 00:10:21.240
Do you want to give it away?

00:10:21.280 --> 00:10:21.460
Yes.

00:10:21.840 --> 00:10:21.960
What?

00:10:22.420 --> 00:10:22.820
No.

00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:24.500
I, however, think...

00:10:24.500 --> 00:10:25.220
I agree, then.

00:10:25.580 --> 00:10:26.300
Shall we start the session?

00:10:26.540 --> 00:10:26.880
Let's start.

00:10:27.460 --> 00:10:28.980
Gentlemen, there is nothing else to do.

00:10:29.180 --> 00:10:29.900
Good afternoon.

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:29.980
Subtitles by the Amara.org community

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:30.960
Good afternoon, Luis.

00:10:31.180 --> 00:10:31.540
Good afternoon.

00:10:32.460 --> 00:10:42.870
What were you recording?

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:44.030
A recording.

00:10:44.680 --> 00:10:47.840
Every day I find it more similar to Don Luis.

00:10:48.550 --> 00:10:49.810
Dignified son of his father.

00:10:49.910 --> 00:10:51.250
Look, Don Gaspar, tonight I...

00:10:51.250 --> 00:10:52.690
Precisely, they told me about the club.

00:10:53.010 --> 00:10:54.550
Tonight they have the game as usual.

00:10:54.730 --> 00:10:56.030
And I assured you it would be leg.

00:10:56.520 --> 00:10:58.320
Impossible, because tonight I...

00:10:58.320 --> 00:10:59.820
Don Miguel, Don Miguel...

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:01.980
There are certain social commitments that can't be avoided.

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:04.680
And it's also an harmless little poker game.

00:11:04.740 --> 00:11:07.220
It's a sedative for the nerves and it wears a lot.

00:11:07.360 --> 00:11:10.760
Well, tonight I'm not going to take any sedative, nor am I going to play.

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:11.590
Do you understand?

00:11:13.930 --> 00:11:14.330
Poker.

00:11:14.350 --> 00:11:16.310
I lost again with Fur, will it be possible?

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:18.040
The last hand I play, huh?

00:11:18.120 --> 00:11:18.560
As you wish.

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:21.420
Boy, tell Mr. Uranio that I'm going to retire.

00:11:21.580 --> 00:11:21.780
Good.

00:11:22.040 --> 00:11:23.210
How much do I owe you?

00:11:24.590 --> 00:11:26.740
Take another, if you've only taken four.

00:11:27.260 --> 00:11:28.000
No, thank you.

00:11:28.520 --> 00:11:29.850
Sir, excuse me.

00:11:30.060 --> 00:11:31.800
Mr. Gorducci will let you know he's retired.

00:11:32.100 --> 00:11:32.580
Thank you.

00:11:33.890 --> 00:11:34.790
Tell me, Polo.

00:11:34.850 --> 00:11:38.480
Are you sure that the boy, Miguel Angel, after the club...

00:11:38.800 --> 00:11:39.900
...will always go home?

00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:42.100
Will he go play somewhere else?

00:11:42.870 --> 00:11:43.830
No, he's going to sleep.

00:11:44.230 --> 00:11:45.160
Are you sure?

00:11:45.480 --> 00:11:48.560
As sure as I've been seeing him since Clarito.

00:11:48.780 --> 00:11:55.720
It's 11 o'clock. I'm going to retire.

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:56.800
How? So early?

00:11:57.160 --> 00:11:57.800
We'll continue tomorrow.

00:11:58.110 --> 00:11:58.970
And? How was that?

00:11:59.190 --> 00:11:59.730
As always.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:00.620
I lost 3,000 pesos.

00:12:00.800 --> 00:12:01.120
Yes, good.

00:12:01.340 --> 00:12:04.100
Where the captain sends, and now to rest, huh?

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:04.620
See you tomorrow.

00:12:04.920 --> 00:12:05.540
See you tomorrow.

00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:09.520
But when do you get here?

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:10.600
Who do you play for?

00:12:10.600 --> 00:12:11.040
For Atlanta?

00:12:11.560 --> 00:12:12.950
You lost your hand today, huh?

00:12:13.370 --> 00:12:13.770
Let's go.

00:12:21.320 --> 00:12:24.300
Just walk around the car, the only one who needs rest is you.

00:12:24.600 --> 00:12:26.680
Tell me, are you going to play somewhere else?

00:12:26.800 --> 00:12:28.560
Look, Mr. Gaspar is afraid that you will lose.

00:12:28.700 --> 00:12:29.260
Yes, I know.

00:12:29.280 --> 00:12:29.960
What he wants is to have the money.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:31.360
And the exclusivity of my losses too.

00:12:31.560 --> 00:12:39.840
Fah, take him home.

00:13:47.884 --> 00:13:48.304
Good night, Jake.

00:14:25.210 --> 00:14:27.840
It's too late, Luisito. It's 12 o'clock.

00:14:27.920 --> 00:14:28.700
I can't get there.

00:14:29.080 --> 00:14:29.860
Why? What are you doing?

00:14:31.520 --> 00:14:33.680
Daddy doesn't want to see you at this hour.

00:14:34.020 --> 00:14:36.540
Last night he challenged me. I cried and everything.

00:14:36.820 --> 00:14:38.300
Did you cry? And for me?

00:14:39.280 --> 00:14:41.780
Bad. Do you like me to cry?

00:14:42.060 --> 00:14:42.740
Yes, for me, yes.

00:14:43.180 --> 00:14:44.800
You know that Daddy is very serious.

00:14:45.040 --> 00:14:46.820
He wants to meet you and that you come in.

00:14:47.120 --> 00:14:49.750
The boyfriends of my two little sisters enter the house.

00:14:50.010 --> 00:14:50.990
But they are going to get married soon.

00:14:51.490 --> 00:14:52.530
And you don't think of getting married?

00:14:52.850 --> 00:14:55.630
Yes, but not so soon. I have to get a job, honest, calm.

00:14:56.110 --> 00:14:59.950
Ah, by the way, Daddy told me that I could get you a job at the factory where...

00:14:59.950 --> 00:14:59.970
Thank you for watching!

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:03.380
Very well, I appreciate it, but the department will get it for me.

00:15:03.440 --> 00:15:05.300
I imagine you don't want to live in a cellar.

00:15:06.100 --> 00:15:06.620
Yes, your brother?

00:15:06.900 --> 00:15:09.620
I could wait for you, thanks to the fact that he was accompanying me until now.

00:15:10.050 --> 00:15:12.170
He's in the kitchen drinking mate, why don't you come in?

00:15:12.370 --> 00:15:13.510
No, what if the old man gets up?

00:15:13.530 --> 00:15:14.650
He's sleeping, come in.

00:15:14.840 --> 00:15:22.210
Well, and that, your father?

00:15:22.430 --> 00:15:23.650
No, my little sister, drink.

00:15:23.910 --> 00:15:25.190
What a lung he gave the guard.

00:15:25.510 --> 00:15:27.450
What are you doing, Rubio?

00:15:27.510 --> 00:15:28.450
What are you saying, Luisito?

00:15:28.740 --> 00:15:29.940
Here, I was waiting for you.

00:15:30.440 --> 00:15:31.480
How did you come so late?

00:15:31.700 --> 00:15:32.260
What did I have to do?

00:15:32.560 --> 00:15:34.700
He's so busy that he can hardly come to see me.

00:15:34.740 --> 00:15:35.860
Don't say that, Margarita.

00:15:38.150 --> 00:15:39.470
Thank you, it's very tasty, I don't want more.

00:15:39.810 --> 00:15:40.650
Don't be so strong.

00:15:41.030 --> 00:15:41.370
Oh, really?

00:15:41.850 --> 00:15:44.750
What if we cut the dream of the old man who gets up at six and sets up the one from San Quintín?

00:15:44.870 --> 00:15:46.210
Well, come on, come on, get up, come on, come on.

00:15:46.450 --> 00:15:50.810
Hey, how do you break your sister?

00:15:51.230 --> 00:15:52.330
No, that's my old man.

00:15:52.720 --> 00:15:54.120
How do you know the station, huh?

00:15:54.700 --> 00:15:55.000
Who's there?

00:15:56.520 --> 00:15:56.760
Nobody.

00:16:00.540 --> 00:16:01.500
Dad woke up.

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:03.740
It's the same way your old man wakes up a regiment.

00:16:04.260 --> 00:16:07.070
Good morning, darling.

00:16:07.450 --> 00:16:08.270
Good morning, Mario.

00:16:08.410 --> 00:16:08.870
What are you doing there?

00:16:09.680 --> 00:16:11.180
Uff, get out of the way, roncoroni.

00:16:11.340 --> 00:16:11.920
Get out of the way.

00:16:12.300 --> 00:16:16.720
What a treasure of girls, huh?

00:16:16.760 --> 00:16:17.240
How do you want?

00:16:17.480 --> 00:16:18.740
Hey, you have to stop that coffee.

00:16:18.960 --> 00:16:21.000
It's not possible that you're singing at three pesos for tango.

00:16:21.060 --> 00:16:22.320
And I do it a little to have fun.

00:16:22.580 --> 00:16:23.360
How to have fun?

00:16:23.540 --> 00:16:25.200
I mean, to have fun while I can't think of anything else.

00:16:25.630 --> 00:16:27.330
Hey, Margarita told me that your old man employs me.

00:16:27.330 --> 00:16:29.270
Ah, if the old man tells you that he employs you, he employs you, huh?

00:16:29.390 --> 00:16:29.930
He employs me.

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:32.080
Come on, Micheline, it's too late.

00:16:32.240 --> 00:16:33.940
The boss must be making a big fuss.

00:16:34.060 --> 00:16:35.400
They have to start at 11, it's more than 12.

00:16:35.720 --> 00:16:36.560
Come on, let's take the bus.

00:16:36.900 --> 00:16:39.140
It's three quarters, we rush the bus and we arrive at the same time.

00:16:39.160 --> 00:16:40.000
At this hour, the bus is worth 20.

00:16:40.300 --> 00:16:41.300
And what are you, Micheline?

00:16:41.540 --> 00:16:42.880
You talk as if you were a millionaire.

00:16:43.220 --> 00:16:43.460
And I'm not.

00:16:43.760 --> 00:16:43.920
What?

00:16:44.240 --> 00:16:45.170
And I'm not the River.

00:16:45.410 --> 00:16:47.420
Well, come on, the boss must be saying,

00:16:47.580 --> 00:16:49.620
why do you think I pay the singer?

00:16:50.140 --> 00:16:51.990
Why do you think I pay the singer?

00:16:52.370 --> 00:16:53.860
To arrive when you want.

00:16:54.460 --> 00:16:55.100
Melon guy.

00:16:56.700 --> 00:16:58.240
Well, put another record.

00:16:58.720 --> 00:16:59.300
Come on, soon.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:00.740
Well...

00:17:00.740 --> 00:17:01.200
You're crazy.

00:17:02.590 --> 00:17:04.880
Come on, let's go to the bathroom.

00:17:13.880 --> 00:17:20.860
Hey, you, power-puncher!

00:17:20.860 --> 00:17:22.530
Maybe you're looking at the toilet,

00:17:22.750 --> 00:17:23.830
and you're making a mess in the bathroom.

00:17:27.580 --> 00:17:28.120
Hey, you, charm!

00:17:28.480 --> 00:17:29.900
How many times have I told you...

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:31.600
Why don't you look at the guys who play the medial?

00:17:31.660 --> 00:17:34.080
I look at whoever I want. If they don't like it, they fire me.

00:17:34.400 --> 00:17:35.420
That's what you think.

00:17:35.800 --> 00:17:36.760
How you've grown.

00:17:37.460 --> 00:17:39.340
When you finish the record, put another one.

00:17:39.540 --> 00:17:40.760
If I want, I'll put it.

00:17:41.840 --> 00:17:42.240
And?

00:17:44.450 --> 00:17:45.050
How about it?

00:17:45.270 --> 00:17:48.830
I ate two queens and in the three simultaneous games I have it ready for the king.

00:17:48.930 --> 00:17:49.810
For the king? I'm glad.

00:17:50.070 --> 00:17:52.170
If you think that this game gives me a loss,

00:17:52.270 --> 00:17:53.610
however, I have it with pleasure.

00:17:53.790 --> 00:17:53.910
Why?

00:17:54.170 --> 00:17:56.830
Because the kings and the queen eat you.

00:17:56.830 --> 00:17:58.730
And I am Republican.

00:18:00.760 --> 00:18:01.460
What do you mean by casualty?

00:18:01.600 --> 00:18:02.500
What casualty?

00:18:02.780 --> 00:18:03.500
What will be served?

00:18:03.900 --> 00:18:05.920
What will be served to celebrate it?

00:18:06.020 --> 00:18:06.300
Thirty!

00:18:06.920 --> 00:18:07.540
A cut.

00:18:07.800 --> 00:18:08.480
A cut?

00:18:09.200 --> 00:18:10.420
What a wasteful table.

00:18:10.780 --> 00:18:12.540
A cut at eight.

00:18:12.800 --> 00:18:13.700
Let it be with milk.

00:18:14.160 --> 00:18:15.160
Be careful.

00:18:15.280 --> 00:18:15.580
Do not bother.

00:18:15.780 --> 00:18:16.060
Do you want?

00:18:16.140 --> 00:18:16.900
Forgive me, man.

00:18:17.100 --> 00:18:17.840
Forgive me.

00:18:18.120 --> 00:18:19.880
Look how everything works that is free.

00:18:20.080 --> 00:18:20.960
The tail of the telephone.

00:18:22.970 --> 00:18:24.410
What are you doing?

00:18:24.570 --> 00:18:24.970
What are you doing?

00:18:25.050 --> 00:18:26.290
But what is that?

00:18:26.530 --> 00:18:27.930
It has to be at eleven and a half.

00:18:27.990 --> 00:18:28.530
It is more than twelve.

00:18:28.850 --> 00:18:29.750
Why do you think I pay you?

00:18:29.750 --> 00:18:29.970
Subtitles by the Amara.org community

00:18:30.090 --> 00:18:32.650
Lately, I have to sing that song because I have so much work to do.

00:18:33.050 --> 00:18:34.530
You're such a troublemaker.

00:18:34.750 --> 00:18:36.420
Hey, Spanish, be careful, okay?

00:18:36.620 --> 00:18:37.760
The singer is going to be my brother-in-law.

00:18:37.980 --> 00:18:38.880
Are you going to marry his sister?

00:18:39.080 --> 00:18:39.500
No, no, no.

00:18:39.600 --> 00:18:40.240
I'm going to marry you.

00:18:40.340 --> 00:18:41.520
No, he's going to marry mine.

00:18:41.860 --> 00:18:42.420
Oh, really?

00:18:42.480 --> 00:18:43.480
I'll withdraw the congratulation.

00:18:43.700 --> 00:18:44.960
Are you going to starve to death?

00:18:44.980 --> 00:18:45.700
Oh, my God.

00:18:49.730 --> 00:18:50.690
Tell me, Mr. Eurípides.

00:18:50.750 --> 00:18:51.050
What is it?

00:18:51.150 --> 00:18:52.170
And the accompaniment you gave me.

00:18:52.630 --> 00:18:54.010
How am I going to sing with a timbre?

00:18:54.170 --> 00:18:55.130
There you have the vitrola.

00:18:55.290 --> 00:18:56.370
Get ready as you can.

00:18:56.470 --> 00:18:58.540
And if you don't want to sing anymore, don't sing.

00:18:58.900 --> 00:18:59.980
Tell me that I sing because I need to.

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:01.900
If not, I wouldn't come to this crazy café to sing.

00:19:02.890 --> 00:19:03.270
Viva!

00:19:03.350 --> 00:19:04.800
Do you always put me the same?

00:19:05.420 --> 00:19:05.860
Well...

00:19:05.860 --> 00:19:26.590
And always the same with its mortise lights

00:19:27.110 --> 00:19:29.550
A cigarette or coffee to wait

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:33.980
The sound of fingers, words with sardines

00:19:33.980 --> 00:19:37.320
And a hope rolling in the billiard

00:19:37.470 --> 00:19:40.640
It's always the same, all the dreams sitting

00:19:41.420 --> 00:19:44.240
I know how to get there, I know what I couldn't do

00:19:44.860 --> 00:19:48.070
And always the same, the busy phone

00:19:48.070 --> 00:19:51.790
Express, march, a cut, handsome, how much is it?

00:19:52.460 --> 00:19:55.200
Wait for Siaco to come to the table

00:19:55.200 --> 00:19:58.410
With triumphs that take a long time to arrive

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:02.380
I wonder if she can paint a head

00:20:02.940 --> 00:20:05.670
A killer never dreams more

00:20:06.250 --> 00:20:09.820
And everything with pretension of kiss

00:20:09.820 --> 00:20:12.880
I remember with a woman's name

00:20:13.540 --> 00:20:16.490
Oh, I also made a verse

00:20:16.490 --> 00:20:20.750
The verse that I will never tell her

00:20:30.640 --> 00:20:37.840
I return to the café, I am no longer who I was,

00:20:37.900 --> 00:20:41.200
I see the years, so sad, what do I do?

00:20:41.500 --> 00:20:44.940
I return to the café and in its wooden table

00:20:44.940 --> 00:20:47.940
I don't have to wait for a new trip to my illusion

00:20:48.780 --> 00:20:51.740
It's always the same, all dreams sitting

00:20:52.420 --> 00:20:56.100
A new author who is looking for a laurel

00:20:56.100 --> 00:20:58.890
And always the same, the telephone occupied

00:20:58.890 --> 00:20:59.710
I'm going to express

00:21:00.540 --> 00:21:01.440
I'm going to make a big cut!

00:21:01.660 --> 00:21:02.900
How much is it?

00:21:03.620 --> 00:21:07.050
Ask for another one!

00:21:07.130 --> 00:21:08.690
They're making a lot of noise for Luisito!

00:21:11.220 --> 00:21:14.070
Not another one!

00:21:14.550 --> 00:21:15.500
Another one at the fair!

00:21:17.640 --> 00:21:18.320
Luisito, I'm sorry!

00:21:18.600 --> 00:21:20.240
This is going to take a while!

00:21:20.440 --> 00:21:23.760
Yes, sir! Just like me!

00:21:24.040 --> 00:21:25.380
We thought you weren't coming today!

00:21:25.440 --> 00:21:26.600
It's a little late, you know?

00:21:26.820 --> 00:21:28.100
Why don't you sing another one?

00:21:28.520 --> 00:21:29.980
This one you just sang is very...

00:21:30.600 --> 00:21:33.620
They'll forgive me for mumbling, but since I'm a poet, I can give my opinion.

00:21:33.720 --> 00:21:35.640
Hey, you idiot, you're going to talk bad about tango, aren't you?

00:21:35.640 --> 00:21:38.640
No, I'll just say that in tango music is a divinity

00:21:38.640 --> 00:21:40.120
and the lyrics a calamity.

00:21:43.480 --> 00:21:44.340
Calm down, please.

00:21:44.840 --> 00:21:46.580
What an atmosphere of sephones.

00:21:46.840 --> 00:21:47.840
I insist, sir.

00:21:48.000 --> 00:21:51.000
We should raise the score by doing more poetry.

00:21:51.320 --> 00:21:51.900
And what do you think?

00:21:52.140 --> 00:21:54.180
What I say is that this thing is going to cut its hair

00:21:54.180 --> 00:21:55.360
if you don't want it to be a hairball.

00:21:55.360 --> 00:21:57.900
I don't know, I don't know.

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:01.360
This was a trick of culture.

00:22:01.660 --> 00:22:04.340
It was done with chess, alchemy.

00:22:04.600 --> 00:22:04.700
Yes, yes.

00:22:13.150 --> 00:22:14.490
Look at that element.

00:22:16.140 --> 00:22:23.360
You have to be honest, Luisito.

00:22:23.500 --> 00:22:23.900
Yes, speak.

00:22:24.120 --> 00:22:26.480
Don't throw the broken bag, what Margarita del Viejo told you.

00:22:26.570 --> 00:22:27.530
It's very shabby.

00:22:27.650 --> 00:22:28.950
They bet you're mysterious.

00:22:29.310 --> 00:22:29.750
And mysterious...

00:22:32.090 --> 00:22:36.280
Margarita didn't dare to tell you, but the old man said he wouldn't let you see you anymore.

00:22:36.420 --> 00:22:37.240
That made me understand.

00:22:37.800 --> 00:22:39.140
But the girl loves you so much.

00:22:39.200 --> 00:22:40.200
And I love her more.

00:22:40.260 --> 00:22:41.420
You don't know how happy I am.

00:22:41.720 --> 00:22:43.640
Of my three sisters, she's the one I love the most.

00:22:43.930 --> 00:22:45.290
She's the one who replaces my late mother.

00:22:45.690 --> 00:22:47.990
Our life is humble, simple, all sincerity.

00:22:48.460 --> 00:22:50.080
And we owe it to her, who is a angel.

00:22:50.590 --> 00:22:54.030
Maybe if you were a bacán, you would be desperate looking for a girl who would love you like her.

00:22:54.250 --> 00:22:55.510
You see that being poor is an advantage.

00:22:55.870 --> 00:22:57.770
If you saw what a fool the slave of life is.

00:22:57.970 --> 00:22:58.650
And what do you know?

00:22:58.850 --> 00:22:59.870
No, tell me, I can imagine.

00:23:00.500 --> 00:23:02.820
Oh, it's late. I have to get up early. I'm going, son.

00:23:03.200 --> 00:23:04.800
No, wait, wait, I'm going to get three more.

00:23:05.380 --> 00:23:08.780
Mr. Neurípides, I'm going to sing another tango.

00:23:09.250 --> 00:23:11.170
Sing the tango to God that you are well.

00:23:11.490 --> 00:23:13.340
And now I'll put you in a quartet.

00:23:13.460 --> 00:23:13.540
Why?

00:23:13.880 --> 00:23:17.110
She just arrived to give me serious. Look at her.

00:23:17.430 --> 00:23:21.820
Bastard! You lied to uncle!

00:23:22.500 --> 00:23:22.820
Exxon.

00:23:23.360 --> 00:23:28.830
In the middle of the tango I'm going to send him a little paper telling him that the letter is mine and that I dedicate it to him.

00:23:28.990 --> 00:23:29.730
They're going to break the ball.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:30.900
Look, there are two, huh?

00:23:31.000 --> 00:23:32.300
One and a half.

00:23:32.920 --> 00:23:35.520
And you, girl, put the tango, this quarter of an hour is over.

00:23:35.520 --> 00:23:38.000
And you, up, huh? Don't fail me.

00:23:38.240 --> 00:23:48.850
I met you a year ago,

00:23:48.850 --> 00:23:50.400
on a dance floor,

00:23:51.220 --> 00:23:53.700
and you were black, fat, I don't even know what you were like.

00:23:54.380 --> 00:23:56.980
What I know is that with the weight that I gathered working,

00:23:57.720 --> 00:23:59.970
I made you wrinkle, I made you flat, I made you...

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:04.400
You have to see the flip-flops that I gave because of your whims

00:24:04.400 --> 00:24:07.680
You have to see the papillones that I passed because of you

00:24:07.680 --> 00:24:11.470
I went to be a monkey clown and to get away from your eyes

00:24:11.470 --> 00:24:15.180
I renounced the whole world and I forgot about everything

00:24:16.020 --> 00:24:22.300
With the watch in my hand I suffered your delay

00:24:23.140 --> 00:24:29.050
And I had the hope that you were going to come back

00:24:30.690 --> 00:24:36.470
But the deadline was fulfilled, that's why I'm shouting to you now

00:24:38.120 --> 00:24:43.020
Your fourth hour is over, may you be well

00:24:43.020 --> 00:24:48.200
And yesterday I am a new man because I live more confident

00:24:48.620 --> 00:24:51.640
Because I know that if you left, it was for the good of my health

00:24:51.640 --> 00:24:54.690
Before I was with the face of terror and bitterness

00:24:55.250 --> 00:24:58.310
Now I live giving joy and youth

00:24:58.310 --> 00:24:59.790
I get up when

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:01.940
and when I want I go to bed

00:25:01.940 --> 00:25:04.340
without asking permission from anyone

00:25:04.340 --> 00:25:05.280
because now I am boss

00:25:05.800 --> 00:25:07.380
without having that torture

00:25:07.380 --> 00:25:09.240
of jealousy and doubt

00:25:09.240 --> 00:25:11.400
that were two black ghosts

00:25:11.400 --> 00:25:12.920
that made a mess of my reason

00:25:12.920 --> 00:25:17.100
with the clock in my hand

00:25:17.100 --> 00:25:20.170
I suffered your delay

00:25:20.990 --> 00:25:23.730
and I had the hope

00:25:23.730 --> 00:25:27.040
that you were going to come back

00:25:27.040 --> 00:25:29.800
but the deadline

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:34.540
Your hour has come

00:25:35.810 --> 00:25:38.170
Your fourth hour is over

00:25:38.170 --> 00:25:38.770
Goodbye!

00:25:39.180 --> 00:25:47.180
You sing very well, huh?

00:25:47.260 --> 00:25:48.580
I kill myself!

00:25:48.890 --> 00:25:50.410
Why do you hit him? You too!

00:26:05.310 --> 00:26:06.350
What are you doing here, ideated woman of life?

00:26:06.610 --> 00:26:07.730
What do you care about here?

00:26:07.770 --> 00:26:17.960
What are you doing here, ideated woman of life?

00:26:33.420 --> 00:26:34.620
Shut up! Shut up!

00:26:34.980 --> 00:26:44.950
I told you it was going to be a mess!

00:26:45.720 --> 00:26:48.200
Oh my God, what a student atmosphere!

00:26:48.820 --> 00:26:50.200
Come on, come on, be careful!

00:26:57.440 --> 00:26:59.660
I find you so agile today, Mr. Gorducci.

00:27:00.060 --> 00:27:01.780
Please, don't remind me of your last name.

00:27:01.940 --> 00:27:02.820
You can't make someone happy.

00:27:04.080 --> 00:27:05.120
Hasn't Mr. Gaspar arrived yet?

00:27:05.460 --> 00:27:08.900
No, he's gone to the bank, but I already told him that you wanted to talk to him urgently.

00:27:09.540 --> 00:27:10.160
There he is.

00:27:10.610 --> 00:27:13.340
Sir, Mrs. Loulou wants to talk to you.

00:27:13.440 --> 00:27:14.560
On the phone? No, personally.

00:27:15.140 --> 00:27:17.160
Tell her that I'm very busy, that I have a meeting at the office.

00:27:17.580 --> 00:27:18.680
One moment!

00:27:19.750 --> 00:27:20.830
Mr. Gaspar is going to have fun.

00:27:21.190 --> 00:27:23.150
He was going to blame me. He has her with me.

00:27:23.400 --> 00:27:24.600
Yesterday he called me a snob.

00:27:24.960 --> 00:27:27.340
How exaggerated. You're not a snob.

00:27:27.600 --> 00:27:29.660
What happens is that you have your face very far back.

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:30.660
Of course, of course.

00:27:30.800 --> 00:27:33.880
Have a good time.

00:27:34.120 --> 00:27:34.600
All right, sir.

00:27:35.780 --> 00:27:38.200
Mr. Gaspar says that a business man like you

00:27:38.200 --> 00:27:40.200
must have a woman like Lulu.

00:27:40.460 --> 00:27:42.300
That kind of girl is out of the question.

00:27:42.300 --> 00:27:44.180
And please don't tell him that tonight

00:27:44.180 --> 00:27:46.280
he's going to marry the Princess of Nylon.

00:27:46.750 --> 00:27:48.490
Speaking of which, what do you think of Lulu?

00:27:49.070 --> 00:27:49.570
The truth.

00:27:49.770 --> 00:27:51.220
Do you want me to tell you the truth?

00:27:51.360 --> 00:27:51.940
Don't be offended.

00:27:52.100 --> 00:27:52.760
No, man, talk.

00:27:55.870 --> 00:27:57.290
She's a divine creature.

00:27:57.890 --> 00:27:59.170
How are you, ma'am?

00:27:59.210 --> 00:27:59.730
I'm delighted.

00:28:00.320 --> 00:28:00.680
And the boys?

00:28:01.000 --> 00:28:02.650
What boys? I don't have any boys.

00:28:03.150 --> 00:28:04.390
But you can have them.

00:28:05.070 --> 00:28:08.180
From what I can see, there's plenty of time to lose.

00:28:08.360 --> 00:28:08.840
How are you?

00:28:09.140 --> 00:28:10.040
Nice to meet you.

00:28:10.240 --> 00:28:12.960
Nice to meet you, and it's been five nights we haven't gone out together.

00:28:13.180 --> 00:28:14.320
And I'm very busy, you see.

00:28:14.720 --> 00:28:15.220
You've lost it.

00:28:15.660 --> 00:28:18.420
I'm here to tell you that I'm going to Punta del Este for a week.

00:28:18.640 --> 00:28:19.320
Do you have any problems?

00:28:19.760 --> 00:28:20.320
I don't have any.

00:28:20.540 --> 00:28:22.250
I would need some money.

00:28:22.710 --> 00:28:23.230
How much?

00:28:24.390 --> 00:28:28.910
Give it to me as a present. It's made of Russian leather.

00:28:29.110 --> 00:28:29.650
And it's very...

00:28:34.840 --> 00:28:37.580
I'll send you a postcard.

00:28:39.060 --> 00:28:39.500
Wonderful!

00:28:40.540 --> 00:28:41.120
It's gold.

00:28:41.420 --> 00:28:42.660
Will you give it to me?

00:28:42.680 --> 00:28:43.680
Yes, see you later.

00:28:43.700 --> 00:28:44.120
Goodbye.

00:28:45.480 --> 00:28:46.850
I congratulate you.

00:28:47.470 --> 00:28:53.180
Well, ladies, but I'm not at the exhibition.

00:28:53.960 --> 00:28:55.060
Bye, Chita.

00:28:55.200 --> 00:28:56.620
I'll take your car to this house.

00:28:56.900 --> 00:28:57.180
Take it.

00:28:57.500 --> 00:28:57.860
Goodbye.

00:29:03.520 --> 00:29:03.880
That's good.

00:29:04.160 --> 00:29:05.000
Who was looking, sir?

00:29:05.280 --> 00:29:06.860
No, I thought it was Picaporte.

